k out the "more"-button in our personal details section to add more details about yourself. Adding "Nationality" and "Birthday" is generally NOT recommended, however it is required in some countries.',b2:"When choosing a photo, make sure it is not older than 2 years.",b3:"Try to choose a photo where your clothing matches the dress code of the desired position (Hint: check out how employees of the company are presenting themselves on  LinkedIn or on the company website).",b4:"Use a professional Email-address. Something along the lines of 'firstname.lastname@gmail.com' cuts it, 'abbygirl129@gmail.com' doesn't. ",b5:"The 'display'-email address you show in your resume and the one for your account don't need to be the same.",b6:"Don't add your Facebook or Instagram, unless you are a professional blogger or social media manager."},profile:{heading:"Summary",b1:"Focus on your motivations, skills and ideas you are able to contribute rather than staying generic.",b2:"Use keywords relevant to your desired position wherever possible in order to pass applicant tracking systems scanning for them.",b3:"Limit yourself to 2-5 short phrases.",b4:"Be as concrete as possible and include tangible facts when writing about yourself."},education:{heading:"Education",b1:"Only list your GPA if it is a) being asked for or b) you managed to get an above-average one.",b2:"When listing your GPA, make sure to include a point of reference for recruiters (e.g. 'GPA 1.1 / 5, Top 5% of class').",b3:"If you didn't graduate (yet), still state achieved credits towards your degree.",b4:"Consider leaving out primary & secondary school.",b5:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},work:{heading:"Professional Experience",b1:"Focus on your achievements rather than your duties.",b2:"Quantify experiences to convey size and/or scale of projects, budgets and results.",b3:"If you use bullets in your description, sort them by importance.",b4:"Use keywords relevant to your desired position wherever possible in order to pass applicant tracking systems scanning for them.",b5:'Use our "Present" option if you are still employed at the company.',b6:"It's best practice to sort your professional experience in chronologically descending order, starting with the most recent entry. We do this automatically for you, but you can still switch things around manually.",b7:'Start your sentences with action words like "created", "developed", "planned", etc.',b8:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},skill:{heading:"Skills",b1:'Try different designs for showing of your skills, like bars or dots under "Design".',b2:"If you want to sort your skills into sub-sections (e.g. soft skills & hard skills), we recommend creating a new custom section.",b3:"Select skills according to your desired position.",b4:'Be specific with skills and add proof if possible, e.g. "Microsoft Office, incl. VBA Macros".'},language:{heading:"Languages",b1:"Make sure to try the available different designs for listing languages, like bars or dots in the Design-Section.",b2:'In "Additional information", try to prove your fluency level. This can be done by including test results or certificates, but also by stating e.g. "lived for 5 months in .."',b3:"Be honest about your language level. ",b4:"If you do not have objective test results at hand, it can help to incorporate examples from past professional experiences where you had to use a foreign language."},interest:{heading:"Interests",b1:"Don't be afraid to list interests on your resume, as they give employers insight into what drives you as a well-rounded individual and might add a further differentiator to your resume.",b2:'Refrain from listing broad, common interests like "meeting friends".',b3:"Avoid listing interests that are related to religion, politics or anything controversial.",b4:"If you have dangerous interests or hobbies, maybe don't put them in your resume.",b5:"Position this section more to the bottom of your resume (definitely after your professional experience and education)."},course:{heading:"Courses",b1:"Past courses shouldn't be the star of the show but rather the icing on the cake. Hence, put this section below your professional experience and education.",b2:"Keep it relevant - only list courses which gave you qualifications that add value to the job for which you are applying.",b3:"Prepare to be quizzed about what you learned during the interview phase, so only put courses in your resume you still know the ins and outs of.",b4:"For added effect, state how you were able to apply the course's content in practice.",b5:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},project:{heading:"Projects",b1:"Mention the size, scope & scale of the project.",b2:"Include project outcomes and what you have learned. ",b3:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},award:{heading:"Awards",b1:'Include tangible facts like the total number of contestants (i.e. "3rd place out of 245 contestants")',b2:"Prove your ability as a team player by mentioning whether you were part of a team.",b3:"Awards can be student competitions, industry accolades or company-wide recognitions for great performance like being nominated for a talent program.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},organisation:{heading:"Organisations",b1:"Mention what you have achieved and learned.",b2:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action.",action:"When writing your description, check our list of"},reference:{heading:"References",b1:"Make sure to brief your references before you put their contact data into your resume.",b2:"Of course, make sure not to include anybody who might say negative things about your past performance.",b3:"Good references include, but are not limited to:",sub:{b31:"Your former boss (either direct or some levels up in the organisation)",b32:"A colleague, either from your department or a department you worked with regularly",b33:"Former teachers or professors",b34:"Business partners directly engaged with",b35:"A contact working at the company you are applying to"},b4:"Refrain from using private references (e.g. friends, family) as they make the impression that you couldn't find professional ones and don't add much value to your resume. "},certificate:{heading:"Certificates",b1:"Include certificates that add value to the job you are applying for (e.g. a driver's license for a sales job).",b2:"Certificates shouldn't be the star of the show but rather the icing on the cake. Hence, put this section below your professional experience and education.",b3:"Certificate titles are usually heavy on acronyms (e.g. CPA for Certified Public Account, CDL for Commercial Driver's license). Make sure to write them out as well."},publication:{heading:"Publications",b1:"Make sure to list all authors of the paper (not only yourself).",b2:"When your academic research of yours isn't published yet, rename this section to e.g. 'Academic Research'.",b3:"If you are not applying to a job where publications are important (e.g. academia), do not use this section. Instead, put your thesis / research into the corresponding education entry."},custom:{heading:"Custom",b1:"Let your creativity flow.",b2:"You might use custom sections to combine several sections.",b3:"Use past tense for your description. Use present tense if you still perform an action."}},uH=e=>{const t=hH[e.section];return t?n("div",{children:Object.keys(t).map((e=>{const l=t[e];return"object"==typeof l?Object.keys(l).map((t=>n(dH,{sub:!0,children:l[t]},`${e}-${t}`))):"heading"===e||"modalHeading"===e?nul